\title{ggcordist: Visualize Distributions of Covariance and Correlation Matrices}
\description{
Visualizes posterior (or prior) draws of covariance and correlation matrices, for example from a 'Stan' fit, using the four-layer approach of Tokuda, Goodrich, Van Mechelen, Gelman and Tuerlinckx, "Visualizing Distributions of Covariance Matrices". The layers are histograms of log standard deviations and correlations, bivariate scatterplots, equiprobability ellipses, and effective variance and effective dependence. Samplers for the Wishart, inverse-Wishart, scaled inverse-Wishart, LKJ and separation strategy distributions are included for reference and for prior-versus-posterior comparisons.
